WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.361
The bike stops answering mid-ride. Before you write to us, Diagnostics shows what

00:00:07.361 --> 00:00:08.664
the browser sees.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.674
The custom ride's bike status is now a button. It opens Diagnostics as a modal

00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:18.717
dialog, and Escape gives the focus back.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.694
With the bike connected: the browser, Web Bluetooth, the page, the bike and its

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:32.047
link, how long it has held, the last command and its acknowledgement, and the

00:00:32.047 --> 00:00:33.534
reconnects this ride.

00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:43.482
With no bike picked, the link facts step aside. With Bluetooth off, it says so, and

00:00:43.482 --> 00:00:45.391
when the bike was last seen.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.604
Four acceptance tests, failing first and passing now, and forty-three new unit tests

00:00:56.604 --> 00:01:00.822
for the facts, the link's history and when the bike was last seen.

00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:09.511
Diagnostics, from a phone to the full screen. Everything stays on this device.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.450
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:19.795 --> 00:01:24.307
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:24.307 --> 00:01:25.978
every hill and interval.

00:01:26.323 --> 00:01:31.501
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:36.949
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:36.949 --> 00:01:39.939
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:40.285 --> 00:01:42.777
A custom workout lives under Profile.
